# CMake build artifacts
cmake-build-*/
build/
out/
CMakeLists.txt.user
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles
CMakeScripts
Testing
Makefile
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json
CTestTestfile.cmake
_deps
CMakeUserPresets.json

# CLion / JetBrains — project settings (.idea) are shared so VCS mappings,
# run configs etc. work for everyone; only user-specific state is ignored.
# See https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
.idea/workspace.xml
.idea/usage.statistics.xml
.idea/tasks.xml
.idea/shelf/
.idea/dictionaries/

# Other IDEs / editors
.vscode/
*.swp

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Compiled shader blobs. The build always compiles SPIR-V itself into
# ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/Shaders and the runtime only ever loads <exe dir>/Shaders,
# so a .spv next to its .vert/.frag source is never read — checking one in only
# risks it going stale against the source it was built from.
*.spv

# Runtime artifacts
*.log
config.json
/.vs
# Any build tree, however it was named. `build-wt/` used to be the only one
# spelled out, and a worktree that configured into `build-<something-else>/`
# committed 45 000 lines of generated CMake and a 63 MB test binary before
# anyone noticed. The pattern costs nothing and `build_errors.txt` (a tracked
# file) is not matched by it — the trailing slash means directories only.
build-*/
build-wt/

# Working screenshots and scratch output. Kept on disk, never committed: these
# are development reference images (some of them screenshots of OTHER engines,
# which have no business in an MIT-licensed public repo) and they put 17 MB into
# every clone, forever, for files nothing in the build or the docs reads.
_shots/
_repro_inc_out.txt
build_errors.txt

# CI build artifacts. They belong on a release, not in git — 145 MB of them were
# committed once and had to be removed by rewriting history. Download them from
# the CI run or the GitHub release instead.
HorizonEditor-linux-x64/
HorizonEditor-macos-arm64/
HorizonEditor-windows-x64/
HorizonEditor-*.zip
HorizonEditor-*.tar.gz
HorizonEditor-*.dmg

# Editor runtime state written next to the exe during local runs.
imgui.ini

# The EngineContent SFTP endpoint for a LOCAL build (host/user/password). This
# repository is public — these values never belong in a tracked file. CI gets
# them from repository secrets instead; see src/HE_ContentSync/CMakeLists.txt.
cmake/EngineContentCredentials.cmake

# Raw downloaded source textures of the auto landscape material (4K Poly Haven /
# ambientCG sets, ~400 MB). The repo has no Git LFS and big binaries were purged
# from history once; where they live for good is still open (docs/auto-landscape-
# material-textures.md §4.4). Stage and pack them with scripts/landscape-textures/.
# CAUTION: ignoring is not enough in EditorDeps/: HorizonEditor's POST_BUILD copies
# the whole folder into every deploy and package_macos.sh copies EditorDeps/Images
# into the .app, so ~400 MB of sources would ride along. Keep them outside the
# repo's EditorDeps/ in the long run (the staging script takes any folder).
EditorDeps/Images/Landscape/

# The landscape texture assets (three 106.7 MiB arrays, 27 single textures) are NOT
# shipped from git: GitHub rejects a push with a file over 100 MiB, and the set would
# double the clone for every re-pack. They live on the EngineContent server and the
# Editor fetches them on demand (docs/auto-landscape-material-textures.md §20).
# A local copy placed here (the one that was uploaded) stays untracked; the
# generator's output (landscape_tex_gen) goes there too, so `git add -A` can't pick
# 750 MiB up by accident.
EditorDeps/EngineContent/Textures/Landscape/*.hasset

# Python bytecode of the helper scripts in scripts/. A .pyc of build_runtimes.py
# was committed once (e68ff8ed) simply because nothing here caught it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
